# Executables keep LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Git converts LF to CRLF on checkout wherever `core.autocrlf=true`, which is the Windows default.
# A shell script with CRLF does not run — bash reports `$'\r': command not found` and refuses
# `set -o pipefail` — so a fresh clone on Windows produces a repository whose own gates cannot
# execute. Nothing in the history is wrong; the checkout is.
#
# Found the first time this repository was materialised fresh on Windows rather than written in
# place, which is late enough to be worth the comment.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
